+// S03-T05: the participant script context fixtures.
+//
+// script-context (unit, Identity scope, no level): the context stack over a
+// standalone registry: nesting and the innermost-only leave, every refusal an
+// entry can meet (forged, unknown and bridge sessions, world and identity
+// scope, wrong party, stale reference, no actor for Self, depth), capture and
+// re-entry as server-internal, re-entry refused after the participant's
+// release, a client-role registry entering nothing.
+//
+// Level fixture (GameState, after the activation fixture; both participant
+// actors live, participant 2 attached on its session):
+//  1 contract:  a fixture-owned Lua probe runs with no context, in
+//               participant 1's server-internal context, in participant 2's
+//               client-intent context and nested (2 inside 1). Each run reads
+//               campaign.* and db.actor and does a harmless action on the
+//               context's actor: a portable-store marker, 1 RU, a news item, a
+//               presentation and a camera effector. Forged, unknown-session,
+//               bridge, stale, wrong-party and world contexts enter nothing.
+//  2 deferred:  a time event created in each context and one outside any
+//               fires in the context it was created in.
+//  3 quests:    the installed mechanic quests are given in each participant's
+//               context through the dialogue entry (participant 2 is offered
+//               mar_base_stalker_tech_task_1, participant 1, who completed it in
+//               S02-T06e, mar_base_stalker_tech_task_2); both stay open
+//               together. Participant 2's fetch item is spawned into actor 2's
+//               inventory; its task reaches the complete stage while
+//               participant 1's does not; participant 2 turns in; the
+//               completion, goodwill, info portion, reward and item removal
+//               land on actor 2 alone. Then participant 1 does the same with
+//               its own task.
+//  4 audit:     the out-of-context db.actor reads counted while two actors
+//               lived (script and line) are written to the capture.
+//
+// CSV rows (s03-t05-script-context.csv):
+//   meta,<p1>,<p2>,<actor1>,<actor2>,<party1>,<party2>,<giver>
+//   probe,<label>,<in_context>,<slot>,<generation>,<origin>,<entry>,<actor>,<db_actor>,<ac_id>,<marker>,<presented>,<effector>,
+//         <money1>,<money2>,<outbox1>,<outbox2>
+//   refusal,<label>,<expected>,<observed>
+//   deferred,<tag>,<fired>,<slot>,<actor>,<db_actor>,<entry>
+//   quest,<label>,<who>,<task>,<native_state>,<owned>,<owner_slot>,<lua_status>,<lua_stage>,<fetch>,<items_self>,
+//         <items_other>,<money_self>,<money_other>,<goodwill_self>,<goodwill_other>,<info_self>,<info_other>,
+//         <outbox_self>,<outbox_other>
+//   outbox,<slot>,<serial>,<kind>,<object>,<detail>
+//   host-read,<site>,<count>
+//   stats,<name>,<value>
+//   check,<phase>,<ok>,<what>
+//   end,<ticks>,<sim_ms>,<wall_ms>,<checks>,<failures>,<phase>,<ok>
